[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: can i trust our crm data? what is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-22 19:55:54\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  7.2s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  7.2s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  7.2s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  7.2s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [ 11.3s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 18.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 18.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 18.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 18.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 18.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 21.2s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.2s] step 1   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.2s] step 1   got hubspot__search (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.2s] step 1   got hubspot__search (7 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.2s] step 1   got hubspot__search (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.2s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 27.1s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 27.1s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 27.1s] step 2   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 28.9s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (9 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 28.9s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (10 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 28.9s] step 2   got hubspot__search (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 28.9s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 31.4s] step 3   got read hubspot.search in full (59 rows) (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.4s] step 3   got read hubspot.companies in full (50 rows) (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.4s] step 4   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 62.3s]          drafting the report from 11 observation(s)\r\n  [100.0s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [100.0s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: skipped, this report asserts no cause (0.0s)\r\n  [113.3s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Can I trust our CRM data? What is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 100s over 4 steps, 50,448 tokens, 11 observations gathered, 8 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The \u2588 deals closed-won this quarter to date ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 total) are structurally complete in HubSpot \u2014 none is missing amount, owner, contacts, or lead source.  [hubspot.closed_won eee09134, hubspot.search 58d51f03, hubspot.search 6b6a2c68, hubspot.search 86e4d2a3, hubspot.search 5cbb2ba8]\r\n  The trust gap is not in the won-deal records but in the accounts behind them: both \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, this quarter's two \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st closed-won accounts, resolve to multiple duplicate company records in the CRM.  [hubspot.companies f4c38111, hubspot.companies 0c323374]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The \u2588 closed-won deals this quarter are structurally complete  (high)\r\n    - Q\u2588-to-date (2026-07-01\u20132026-09-22) closed-won deals total \u2588, worth $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 combined: \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588k), \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588k), \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 - Self-hosted ($\u2588\u2588\u2588k), and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588k).  [hubspot.closed_won eee09134]\r\n    - None of these \u2588 closed-won deals is missing amount, owner, associated contacts, or lead source \u2014 targeted searches for closed-won deals in this window lacking each of those fields all returned zero results.  [hubspot.search 58d51f03, hubspot.search 6b6a2c68, hubspot.search 86e4d2a3, hubspot.search 5cbb2ba8]\r\n  Duplicate company records exist for at least one closed-won account, risking attribution and reporting errors  (medium)\r\n    - The closed-won \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal is tied to a company named '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588', but a company search for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' returns \u2588 separate company records (two named exactly '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' on domains \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, plus a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 reseller record and an unnamed record on domain \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588), any of which the deal could have been associated with.  [hubspot.closed_won eee09134, hubspot.companies f4c38111]\r\n    - Si\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588rly, a search for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' \u2014 the account behind the $\u2588\u2588\u2588k closed-won '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 - Self-hosted' deal \u2014 surfaces two distinct company records both literally named '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' (ids \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 on \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, lifecycle 'customer', and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 on \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, lifecycle 'lead'), alongside dozens of unrelated '*\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588*' matches, making it ambiguous which company record the revenue rolls up to.  [hubspot.closed_won eee09134, hubspot.companies 0c323374]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [contradicted] Closed-won deals this quarter are missing key fields (amount, owner, contacts, source) the way some closed-lost deals are.\r\n      Explicit field-presence searches restricted to closed-won deals in the window returned zero matches for each of the four checks, so the field-completeness concern that motivated the question does not apply to the won deals themselves.\r\n  [supported] Duplicate/ambiguous company records for major closed-won accounts (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) could cause revenue or attribution to be double-counted or misassigned in CRM rollups.\r\n      Both accounts behind this quarter's two \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st closed-won deals resolve to multiple company records rather than one canonical record, which is a structural CRM inconsistency independent of the deal records themselves being complete.\r\n  [contradicted] Data quality issues are uniform across won and lost deals, so trusting closed-won totals is no different from trusting the full pipeline.\r\n      The lost-deal set contains null-source and zero-contact records not found anywhere in the won-deal set, so completeness is not uniform: the won total can be trusted at face value while the broader pipeline data (used for source/attribution analysis) cannot.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Merge the duplicate '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' and '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' company records in HubSpot before running quarterly revenue-by-account or logo-count reports.\r\n      why: Both accounts anchor this quarter's \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st closed-won deals ($\u2588\u2588k and $\u2588\u2588\u2588k); leaving duplicate records in place risks under- or over-counting these accounts in account-level reporting even though the deal records themselves are complete.\r\n      [hubspot.closed_won eee09134, hubspot.companies f4c38111, hubspot.companies 0c323374]\r\n  P\u2588 Backfill or flag the null source/source_detail on the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost deals, and review why \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 has zero associated contacts despite reaching closed-lost.\r\n      why: These are the only gaps found in the quarter's deal data, and they sit in the lost-deal set that source/channel attribution analyses rely on.\r\n      [hubspot.search 448b4e6e]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Company deduplication was checked only for the two named accounts investigated (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588); other closed-won or pipeline accounts may have the same duplicate-record issue and were not checked.\r\n  - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company search returned only \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 matching company records (paginated), so the true count and nature of \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-related duplicates could be \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588r than observed.\r\n  - This is a quarter-to-date window (through 2026-09-22, \u2588 days before quarter end); more deals may still close and shift the completeness picture for Q\u2588 as a whole.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company search returned a digest over \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 total matching rows; the remaining \u2588\u2588 were not enumerated, so the full extent of \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-related duplicate/near-duplicate company records is not fully confirmed.\r\n  - The reporting window (2026-07-01 to 2026-09-22) is quarter-to-date, not a completed quarter; totals for closed-won and closed-lost deals may still change before 2026-09-30.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  eee09134  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2026-07-01..2026-09-22\r\n  f4c38111  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  0c323374  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  58d51f03  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!amount?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  6b6a2c68  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!hubspot_owner_id?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  86e4d2a3  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_won=true&num_associated_contacts=0\r\n  5cbb2ba8  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!hs_analytics_source?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  448b4e6e  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (113s wall, 110s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1      7.1    6%     7.1  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      4.1    4%     4.1  in 0 out 0\r\n  \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_model       4     46.9   41%    11.7  in 8 out 3,788 cached 41,424\r\n  \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_tools       3      4.1    4%     1.4  in 0 out 0\r\n  draft            1     37.7   33%    37.7  in 42,725 out 3,927\r\n  gate             1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  verify           1     10.5    9%    10.5  in 43,280 out 1,421\r\n  sufficiency      1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  unmeasured              2.8    2%\r\n  cache hit rate: 33%\r\n"]
